 "inference": [
  "Control and Mobility are the site's formulas term for term, with the same inputs. Control does not read RateOfFire.",
  "Hipfire: the 1.2 is applied inside the root, which equals the site's sqrt(1.2) factor. It is chosen by comparing IncreasePerShotFraction with the constant 1.0, so the site's rule (factor applies when the fraction is not 1) is consistent with a not-equal, less-than or greater-than test; the direction is not read.",
  "Hipfire uses the 18-entry table only when a test on MinAngleIndex passes; otherwise it uses the MinAngle input directly. The index is clamped to 0..17 before the lookup.",
  "None of the seven graphs clamps its result. The site's min(100) for Hipfire is not in the graph; if the game limits the bar it does so elsewhere.",
  "Arithmetic function meanings (multiply, add, divide, power) follow from the Control graph reproducing the known formula. Sine, tangent and square root are the functions that make the formulas match the panels; their hashes are not independently named."
 ],
